The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
modes = kzalloc_objs(*modes, connector_count);
...
if (!crtcs || !modes || !enabled || !offsets) {
    ret = -ENOMEM;
    goto out;
}
...
out:
    modes_destroy(dev, modes, connector_count);
```
Reason:
When `kzalloc_objs` fails for `modes`, the pointer remains NULL. The error check jumps to label `out`, where `modes_destroy` is called unconditionally. This function dereferences the NULL pointer, causing a NULL pointer dereference.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (modes)
    modes_destroy(dev, modes, connector_count);
```
Reason:
Adding a NULL check before calling `modes_destroy` ensures that the function is only invoked when `modes` is non-NULL, preventing the dereference of a NULL pointer in the error path.

